  "question": {
    "text": "If $m$ and $e$ are the mass and charge of the revolving electron in the orbit of radius $r$ for hydrogen atom, the total energy of the revolving electron will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XxuLu",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2} \\frac{e^2}{r}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BMShW",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{e^2}{r}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jVtcw",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{m e^2}{r}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BG3fS",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{1}{2} \\frac{e^2}{r}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Total energy of a revolving electron is the sum of its kinetic and potential energy. Total energy $=$ K.E. $+$ P. E.\n$$\n=\\frac{e^2}{2 r}+\\left(-\\frac{e^2}{r}\\right)=-\\frac{e^2}{2 r}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
